{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773076026,"nonce":"yNHJqxnrivtnTSN17WWhmUWrX9A=","title":"console-view layout: send row cut off; body scrolls instead of stream-renderer","message":"When in rich view, the entire page body scrolls, pushing the send row below the visible area. Root causes: (1) .app-shell uses min-height:100vh with no overflow:hidden, so body can grow past viewport. (2) .app-content has padding 28px top + 48px bottom with no flex/height constraint, so .console-view height:calc(100vh-80px) overflows the viewport. Fix: app-shell → height:100vh+overflow:hidden; app-content → flex:1+min-height:0+overflow-y:auto; add app-content--console modifier (padding:0, overflow:hidden) when console tab is active; console-view → flex:1 instead of fixed calc height.","files":null}]}